decisions:
  - id: shared-camera-arch
    decision: Single SharedCameraSession with CameraFrameConsumer protocol instead of per-provider AVCaptureSessions
    rationale: macOS only allows one AVCaptureSession per camera device — dual sessions caused conflicts. Shared session distributes CVPixelBuffers to all registered consumers via weak references.
  - id: native-vision-gaze
    decision: Replace MediaPipeGazeProvider (Python subprocess) with VisionGazeProvider (Apple Vision framework)
    rationale: Eliminates Python dependency, runs natively on Apple Silicon, shares camera frames with gesture provider, uses VNDetectFaceLandmarksRequest for pupil + eyebrow extraction.
  - id: continuous-voice-mode
    decision: Auto-start continuous 4-second chunk recording when voice is toggled on
    rationale: Push-to-talk required eyebrow trigger which users may not have configured. Continuous mode feeds speech directly to buffer without manual control.
  - id: generic-bracket-strip
    decision: Strip all [bracketed] tokens generically instead of hardcoded list
    rationale: WhisperKit outputs many token variants ([BLANK_AUDIO], [inaudible], [NOISE], etc.) in mixed case. Generic stripping catches all current and future tokens.
  - id: zone-router-dispatch
    decision: dispatchToTarget() prefers gazeZoneRouter.targetedInstance over gazeRouter.currentTarget
    rationale: Workspace-managed instances are targeted via GazeZoneRouter but the ManagedInstance.instance may be nil before AX detection, leaving gazeRouter.currentTarget nil. Both paths must be checked.
errors_encountered:
